
  riscvsim › demo 4 · Guessing wrong
  A branch guesses, misses, and wrong work is thrown away.

   1  # The pipeline guesses where a branch goes before it
   2  # knows. A wrong guess throws away what came in behind it.
   3  addi x1, x0, 3     # run the loop 3 times
   4  addi x2, x0, 0
   5  loop:
   6  addi x2, x2, 1     # count each pass
   7  addi x1, x1, -1
   8  bne  x1, x0, loop  # guessed, then checked in EX
   9  addi x3, x0, 99    # after the loop

  cycle 1
    IF addi x1, x0, 3  ID ·  EX ·  MEM ·  WB ·
    › The first instruction, addi, is fetched from memory.

  cycle 2
    IF addi x2, x0, 0  ID addi x1, x0, 3  EX ·  MEM ·  WB ·
    › addi is decoded and reads its source registers.

  cycle 3
    IF addi x2, x2, 1  ID addi x2, x0, 0  EX addi x1, x0, 3  MEM ·  WB ·
    › addi is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 4
    IF addi x1,x1,-1  ID addi x2,x2,1  EX addi x2,x0,0  MEM addi x1,x0,3  WB ·
    › addi is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 5
    IF bne x1,x0…  ID addi x1,x1…  EX addi x2,x2…  MEM addi x2…  WB addi x1…
    ✓ x1 = 3
    › addi needs x2 from addi, so it is forwarded from the EX/MEM latch and
      nobody waits.

  cycle 6
    IF addi x3,x0…  ID bne x1,x0…  EX addi x1,x1…  MEM addi x2…  WB addi x2…
    ✓ x2 = 0
    › addi finishes and writes x2 = 0.

  cycle 7
    IF ·  ID ✗ addi x3,x0…  EX bne x1,x0…  MEM addi x1,x1,-1  WB addi x2,x2,1
    ✓ x2 = 1
    ✗ The branch was wrong (bne was guessed not taken, but it was taken), so
      one instruction was thrown away.

  cycle 8
    IF addi x2,x2,1  ID flushed  EX flushed  MEM bne x1,x0…  WB addi x1,x1,-1
    ✓ x1 = 2
    › addi finishes and writes x1 = 2.

  cycle 9
    IF addi x1,x1,-1  ID addi x2,x2,1  EX flushed  MEM flushed  WB bne x1,x0…
    › addi is decoded and reads its source registers.

  cycle 10
    IF bne x1,x0…  ID addi x1,x1,-1  EX addi x2,x2,1  MEM flushed  WB flushed
    › addi is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 11
    IF addi x2,x2…  ID bne x1,x0…  EX addi x1,x1…  MEM addi x2,x2…  WB flushed
    › addi is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 12
    IF addi x1,x1…  ID addi x2,x2…  EX bne x1,x0…  MEM addi x1…  WB addi x2…
    ✓ x2 = 2
    › bne needs x1 from addi, so it is forwarded from the EX/MEM latch and
      nobody waits.

  cycle 13
    IF bne x1,x0…  ID addi x1,x1…  EX addi x2,x2…  MEM bne x1,x0…  WB addi x1…
    ✓ x1 = 1
    › addi finishes and writes x1 = 1.

  cycle 14
    IF addi x2,x2…  ID bne x1,x0…  EX addi x1,x1…  MEM addi x2…  WB bne x1,x0…
    › addi is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 15
    IF ✗ addi x1…  ID ✗ addi x2…  EX bne x1,x0…  MEM addi x1,x1…  WB addi x2…
    ✓ x2 = 3
    ✗ The branch was wrong (bne was guessed taken, but it fell through), so
      two instructions were thrown away.

  cycle 16
    IF addi x3,x0,99  ID flushed  EX flushed  MEM bne x1,x0…  WB addi x1,x1,-1
    ✓ x1 = 0
    › addi finishes and writes x1 = 0.

  cycle 17
    IF ·  ID addi x3, x0, 99  EX flushed  MEM flushed  WB bne x1, x0, loop
    › addi is decoded and reads its source registers.

  cycle 18
    IF ·  ID ·  EX addi x3, x0, 99  MEM flushed  WB flushed
    › addi is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 19
    IF ·  ID ·  EX ·  MEM addi x3, x0, 99  WB flushed
    › Nothing is left to fetch, so the pipeline is emptying.

  cycle 20
    IF ·  ID ·  EX ·  MEM ·  WB addi x3, x0, 99
    ✓ x3 = 99
    ✓ addi writes x3 = 99, and the program is finished.

  ✓ 20 cycles · 12 instructions · CPI 1.67 · 0 stalls · 2 mispredictions
    Ends with x1 = 0 · x2 = 3 · x3 = 99
    Why it slowed down:
    • The branch was wrong (bne was guessed not taken, but it was taken), so
      one instruction was thrown away.
    • The branch was wrong (bne was guessed taken, but it fell through), so
      two instructions were thrown away.

